  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Unit of force is written as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Now, torque can be written as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></math>&nbsp;therefore its unit can be written as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Pressure is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac></math>, therefore unit of pressure will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Now, pressure gradient is given by ratio of pressure and distance, so its unit will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Impulse is given by product of force and time, so its unit will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>As we know unit of torque and energy is the same, therefore energy density can written as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>energy</mtext><mtext>volume</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p>"
  }
